# Terminal Kit Free Distribution License 1.0

## 1. Scope

Each copyright holder who offers material under this license is a Licensor.

Covered Material means Terminal Kit code, styles, documentation, and other material offered under this license. It includes copies and derivative modifications, forks, components, and themes, to the extent that they contain or derive from that material.

Third-party dependencies and assets retain their own licenses. Independently created material that contains no Covered Material retains its own terms.

An Application is a separate product whose main purpose is functionality other than supplying reusable UI components, libraries, frameworks, themes, or their derivatives. Games, business applications, and websites can be Applications. Calling a component kit an application, or adding a demonstration around it, does not make it an Application.

## 2. Permissions

Each Licensor grants you a worldwide, nonexclusive, royalty-free copyright license to use, run, copy, modify, and distribute their Covered Material, subject to these conditions.

You may create and distribute free forks, modified components, and derived themes. This permission includes free alternatives to Terminal Kit.

You may use and modify Covered Material inside free or paid Applications. You may charge for the Application, subscriptions, advertising, or its independent functionality. You may distribute Covered Material as part of that Application, including compiled or bundled forms.

Your independently created Application code may use different terms and remain private. This license does not require publication of your Application or private changes that you do not distribute.

## 3. Free distribution of Covered Material

You must not charge for a license, copy, download, access, or redistribution of Covered Material as a component, library, framework, theme, or other reusable toolkit product. This condition applies to original and modified versions, forks, subsets, and derived component or theme packs.

You must not place Covered Material behind a mandatory payment, paid membership, or paid bundle when the product supplies that material for reuse. Describing the charge as support, a donation, packaging, hosting, or another service does not permit a required payment for access to that product.

The paid Application permission in section 2 remains available. An Application may include or internally expose component interfaces needed for its operation. Incidental availability of its bundled code does not make it a toolkit product. Offering reusable Covered Material as a paid SDK, add-on, or theme product is subject to this section.

You may accept voluntary donations. Access to and use of Covered Material must not depend on the donation.

You may charge for separate implementation, customization, maintenance, consulting, or training work. Those fees must pay for the work, not a right to receive or reuse a toolkit product. Any Covered Material delivered through that work retains this license and the recipient's free redistribution rights.

## 4. Preserve these rights

Every copy of Covered Material that you distribute must carry this license and its existing copyright and attribution notices. Identify your modifications without removing earlier notices.

You must offer your distributed derivative Covered Material under these same terms. You must not replace these terms with terms that permit selling that Covered Material as a toolkit product or restrict the permissions granted here.

Recipients receive the same permissions directly from each applicable Licensor. You must not impose a royalty or another charge for exercising those permissions. Your Application's separate terms must identify Covered Material as an exception and preserve these permissions for that material.

This condition applies to Covered Material, not to independently created Application code, independent works, or third-party material under separate licenses.

## 5. Continuing permissions

These permissions continue for the duration of the applicable copyright and are irrevocable while you comply with these terms. A later license or policy change does not withdraw permissions already granted under this license.

Covered Material and its distributed derivatives remain available for free redistribution under these terms. A distributor cannot turn those copies into a paid toolkit license.

These terms govern copies offered under this license. They do not revoke rights previously granted under another license.

## 6. Violations

Your permissions end if you violate these conditions. For a first violation, they automatically resume if you correct it within 30 days after receiving notice. This restoration does not erase liability for the violation.

## 7. Other rights

This license does not transfer ownership or grant trademark rights. You may preserve names for attribution without implying endorsement. It does not limit rights that applicable law gives you independently of this license.

Each Licensor also grants a royalty-free patent license for claims they control that are necessarily infringed by their Covered Material as supplied. This grant does not cover claims infringed only by your independent additions. Your patent grant from a Licensor ends if you bring a patent claim alleging that their Covered Material infringes your patent.

## 8. Warranty and liability

To the extent applicable law permits, Licensors provide Covered Material without warranties, including warranties of merchantability, fitness for a purpose, or noninfringement. You accept the risks of using it. Licensors are not liable for loss or damages from its use or distribution, except where law requires otherwise.
